TestData/weapons/README describes.

tf_weapon_breakable_sign: the Neon Annihilator and its Promo skin
(items_working.tsv:813, :834), the melee held as the equipped item whose
class is its own row (TFSharedDefs's TF_WEAPON_BREAKABLE_SIGN), for the
works rows' kind and catalogue facts (TFWeaponKinds.Of's melee answer, the
plasma fade the kill stamps beside it). Extracted and trimmed exactly as
TestData/weapons/README describes.

tf_weapon_mechanical_arm: the Short Circuit (items_working.tsv:164), the
engineer's secondary whose trigger is the shock attack (TFWeaponKinds.Of's
MechanicalArm id, TFMechanicalArmFacts' gates, the orb entity). Rows only
where stock's C++ states them - the pack's .ctx waits with the extraction
(tools/vpk-extract refused this session); the primary's purse is the
mod_ammo_per_shot hook no side carries yet.

tf_weapon_charged_smg: the Cleaner's Carbine's row (items_working.tsv:751),
the charged SMG whose alt-fire spends the boost meter on the mini-crit buff
(TFWeaponBehaviour's ChargedSmg arm, the boost facts; stock
CTFChargedSMG, tf_weapon_smg.cpp). Built on the SMG's block, the spread and
brass the Carbine's shipped schema names. Extracted and trimmed exactly as
TestData/weapons/README describes.

tf_weapon_handgun_scout_primary: the Shortstop (items_working.tsv:220), the
scout's four-pellet pistol whose alt-fire is the shove (CTFPistol_ScoutPrimary,
tf_weapon_pistol.cpp), for the shove facts' press (TFWeaponBehaviour's
HandgunScoutPrimary arm). Extracted and trimmed exactly as
TestData/weapons/README describes.

tf_weapon_shotgun_building_rescue: the Rescue Ranger (items_working.tsv:997),
the engineer's shotgun whose shot is the repair bolt (TFWeaponKinds.Of's
Projectile row, TFProjectileEffects' BuildingRepairBolt case over the
arrow entity, TFArrow's BuildingHealingArrow arm). Extracted and trimmed
exactly as TestData/weapons/README describes.

tf_weapon_parachute: The B.A.S.E. Jumper's own row (items_working.tsv:312),
the soldier's and demoman's equipped secondary whose shipped script is the
fist-shaped melee block (TFWeaponKinds.Of's melee answer through WeaponType,
the parachute pair riding the movement hook's AirJump check), for the works
